    "title": "Reinhardt's Hanson named AAC Special Teams Player of the Week - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By gcallaghan ,\n18 hours ago Alex Hanson Reinhardt kicker Alex Hanson was named the Appalachian Athletic Conference Special Teams Player of the Week after his performance in the Eagles’ 56-0 win over Rio Grande on Saturday.\nIt marked the fourth time Hanson has won the award this season and the sixth time this season a Reinhardt player has taken a weekly award from the conference. Quarterback Taylor Jackson and defensive back Braylon Jones earned Player of the Week honors in Weeks 1 and 3, respectively.\nHanson, a sophomore from Peachtree Ridge High School, accounted for eight points in the Eagles’ victory, going a perfect 8-for-8 on extra point attempts. He also punted twice for an average of 43.5 yards, with a long of 48, while placing one of those punts inside the Rio Grande 20-yard line.\nHanson is 34-for-35 overall on points-after this year, with an 8-for-10 clip on field goals with 58 total points. His longest field goal of the season came from 47 yards away.\nHanson is 3-for-4 on field goals and 22-of-23 on extra points since conference play began.",
